# tsc -b emits these from vite.config.ts on every `npm run build` (tsconfig.node.json
# is a composite project with no noEmit). Vite's config loader prefers .js over .ts
# when both exist, so a committed, possibly-stale .js silently wins over source edits
# in `npm run dev` — regenerate locally, never commit.
vite.config.js
vite.config.d.ts
